Oracle::initialize(address _admin)
└── Given valid admin
    ├── It should grant ADMIN_ROLE to admin
    └── It should grant ORACLE_MANAGER_ROLE to admin

Oracle::updateUsdFeedInfo(address _token, address _priceFeed, uint256 _stalenessInterval)
├── Given caller has ADMIN_ROLE
│   ├── When price feed is zero address
│   │   └── It should revert with OracleZeroAddress
│   ├── When staleness interval is zero
│   │   └── It should revert with OracleZeroStalenessInterval
│   ├── When token is not yet supported (first USD-feed registration)
│   │   ├── When price feed decimals > 18
│   │   │   ├── It should revert with OracleInvalidFeedDecimals
│   │   │   └── It should NOT add token to supported tokens set
│   │   ├── When price feed decimals <= 18
│   │   │   ├── It should add token to supported tokens set (token registration)
│   │   │   ├── It should set USD price feed and staleness interval
│   │   │   ├── It should increment supported token count
│   │   │   └── It should emit UsdFeedAdded event
│   │   ├── When price feed has exactly 18 decimals
│   │   │   ├── It should register the token
│   │   │   └── It should return the already-normalized price (2000e18)
│   │   └── When token is address(0) (native ETH)
│   │       ├── It should register native ETH as supported
│   │       └── It should set USD price feed and staleness interval
│   └── When token is already supported (updating existing USD feed)
│       ├── When price feed and staleness interval are unchanged
│       │   └── It should revert with OracleNothingToUpdate
│       ├── When only the price feed is changed
│       │   ├── When new price feed decimals > 18
│       │   │   ├── It should revert with OracleInvalidFeedDecimals
│       │   │   └── It should leave original price feed unchanged
│       │   └── When new price feed decimals <= 18
│       │       ├── It should update price feed
│       │       └── It should emit UsdFeedUpdated event
│       ├── When only the staleness interval is changed
│       │   ├── It should update staleness interval
│       │   └── It should emit UsdStalenessIntervalUpdated event
│       └── When both price feed and staleness interval are changed
│           ├── It should update price feed
│           ├── It should update staleness interval
│           ├── It should emit UsdFeedUpdated event
│           └── It should emit UsdStalenessIntervalUpdated event
└── Given caller does not have ADMIN_ROLE
    └── It should revert (AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount)

Oracle::removeToken(address _token)
├── Given caller has ADMIN_ROLE
│   ├── When token is supported
│   │   ├── It should clear outbound pair feeds and emit PairFeedRemoved for each
│   │   ├── It should clear inbound pair feeds that quote this token
│   │   ├── It should remove token from supported tokens set
│   │   ├── It should emit TokenRemoved event
│   │   └── It should decrease supported token count
│   ├── When token is not supported
│   │   └── It should revert with OracleTokenNotSupported
│   └── When token is address(0) (native ETH)
│       ├── It should remove native ETH from supported tokens
│       └── It should emit TokenRemoved event
└── Given caller does not have ADMIN_ROLE
    └── It should revert (AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount)

Oracle::getUsdPrice(address _token)
├── Given token is supported
│   ├── When price feed returns a valid, non-stale price
│   │   ├── It should return normalized price (18 decimals)
│   │   └── It should return updatedAt as the timestamp
│   ├── When price is stale (exceeds token staleness interval)
│   │   └── It should revert with OracleStalePrice
│   ├── When answer <= 0 (negative price)
│   │   └── It should revert with OracleInvalidPrice
│   ├── When updatedAt == 0 (no round data)
│   │   └── It should revert with OracleNoRoundData
│   ├── When updatedAt > block.timestamp (future timestamp)
│   │   └── It should revert with OracleInvalidTimestamp
│   ├── When updatedAt == block.timestamp
│   │   └── It should return price and timestamp successfully
│   └── When the price feed uses 18 decimals
│       └── It should return the price already normalized to 18 decimals
└── Given token is not supported
    └── It should revert with OracleTokenNotSupported

Oracle::getUsdPriceWithStalenessCheck(address _token, uint256 _maxStaleness)
├── Given token is supported
│   ├── When price is within _maxStaleness
│   │   └── It should return normalized price (18 decimals)
│   ├── When _maxStaleness is larger than the token's staleness interval
│   │   └── It should return the price using _maxStaleness
│   ├── When _maxStaleness is stricter than the token's staleness interval
│   │   └── It should return the price using _maxStaleness
│   ├── When price is stale (exceeds _maxStaleness)
│   │   └── It should revert with OracleStalePrice
│   ├── When updatedAt == 0
│   │   └── It should revert with OracleNoRoundData
│   └── When updatedAt > block.timestamp
│       └── It should revert with OracleInvalidTimestamp
└── Given token is not supported
    └── It should revert with OracleTokenNotSupported

Oracle::convertTokenToUSD(address _token, uint256 _amount, uint8 _inputDecimals)
├── Given token is supported
│   ├── When inputs are valid and price is fresh
│   │   ├── It should normalize input amount to 18 decimals
│   │   ├── It should multiply normalized amount by normalized price
│   │   └── It should return USD amount in 18 decimals
│   ├── When _inputDecimals differ from 18 (e.g. 8)
│   │   └── It should normalize the amount before converting
│   ├── When the price feed uses 18 decimals
│   │   └── It should convert correctly
│   ├── When price is stale
│   │   └── It should revert with OracleStalePrice
│   ├── When answer <= 0 (invalid price)
│   │   └── It should revert with OracleInvalidPrice
│   ├── When updatedAt == 0
│   │   └── It should revert with OracleNoRoundData
│   └── When updatedAt > block.timestamp
│       └── It should revert with OracleInvalidTimestamp
└── Given token is not supported
    └── It should revert with OracleTokenNotSupported

Oracle::convertUsdToToken(address _token, uint256 _amount, uint8 _outputDecimals)
├── Given token is supported
│   ├── When inputs are valid and price is fresh
│   │   ├── It should divide USD amount by normalized price
│   │   ├── It should unnormalize result to _outputDecimals
│   │   └── It should return token amount with _outputDecimals
│   ├── When _outputDecimals differ from 18 (e.g. 8)
│   │   └── It should unnormalize the result to _outputDecimals
│   ├── When price is stale
│   │   └── It should revert with OracleStalePrice
│   ├── When answer <= 0 (invalid price)
│   │   └── It should revert with OracleInvalidPrice
│   ├── When updatedAt == 0
│   │   └── It should revert with OracleNoRoundData
│   └── When updatedAt > block.timestamp
│       └── It should revert with OracleInvalidTimestamp
└── Given token is not supported
    └── It should revert with OracleTokenNotSupported

Oracle::convert(address _tokenIn, address _tokenOut, uint256 _amountIn, uint8 _inputDecimals, uint8 _outputDecimals)
├── Given both tokens are supported
│   ├── When a direct pair feed (_tokenIn / _tokenOut) is registered
│   │   ├── When the pair feed is fresh
│   │   │   ├── It should convert using the pair price (amountIn * pairPrice)
│   │   │   ├── It should prefer the pair feed over the USD cross-rate
│   │   │   ├── It should normalize _amountIn from _inputDecimals before converting
│   │   │   └── It should unnormalize the result to _outputDecimals
│   │   └── When the pair feed is stale
│   │       └── It should revert with OracleStalePrice (no silent USD fallback)
│   ├── When only an inverted pair feed (_tokenOut / _tokenIn) is registered
│   │   └── It should convert using the inverse of the inverted pair price
│   ├── When no pair feed is registered
│   │   ├── When prices are fresh
│   │   │   ├── It should return amountIn * priceIn / priceOut as a single USD cross-rate
│   │   │   ├── It should normalize _amountIn from _inputDecimals before converting
│   │   │   ├── It should unnormalize the result to _outputDecimals
│   │   │   └── It should agree with chained convertTokenToUSD -> convertUsdToToken for round prices
│   │   ├── When the input feed is stale
│   │   │   └── It should revert with OracleStalePrice
│   │   └── When the output feed is stale
│   │       └── It should revert with OracleStalePrice
│   ├── When a pair feed is removed after registration
│   │   └── It should fall back to the USD cross-rate
│   └── When _tokenIn equals _tokenOut
│       └── It should only convert decimals (no feed reads beyond support checks)
├── Given _tokenIn is not supported
│   └── It should revert with OracleTokenNotSupported
└── Given _tokenOut is not supported
    └── It should revert with OracleTokenNotSupported

Oracle::updatePairFeedInfo(address _tokenA, address _tokenB, address _priceFeed, uint256 _stalenessInterval)
├── Given caller has ADMIN_ROLE
│   ├── When _tokenA equals _tokenB
│   │   └── It should revert with OracleIdenticalTokens
│   ├── When either token is not USD-supported
│   │   └── It should revert with OracleTokenNotSupported
│   ├── When price feed is zero address
│   │   └── It should revert with OracleZeroAddress
│   ├── When staleness interval is zero
│   │   └── It should revert with OracleZeroStalenessInterval
│   ├── When pair is not registered (new pair)
│   │   ├── When price feed decimals > 18
│   │   │   ├── It should revert with OracleInvalidFeedDecimals
│   │   │   └── It should NOT register the pair
│   │   └── When price feed decimals <= 18
│   │       ├── It should store the pair feed and staleness interval
│   │       ├── It should report isPairSupported as true
│   │       └── It should emit PairFeedAdded event
│   └── When pair is already registered (updating)
│       ├── When price feed and staleness interval are unchanged
│       │   └── It should revert with OracleNothingToUpdate
│       └── When feed and/or staleness change
│           ├── It should update the stored values
│           ├── It should emit PairFeedUpdated when the feed changes
│           └── It should emit PairStalenessIntervalUpdated when staleness changes
└── Given caller does not have ADMIN_ROLE
    └── It should revert (AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount)

Oracle::removePairFeedInfo(address _tokenA, address _tokenB)
├── Given caller has ADMIN_ROLE
│   ├── When pair is registered
│   │   ├── It should clear the pair feed
│   │   ├── It should report isPairSupported as false
│   │   └── It should emit PairFeedRemoved event
│   └── When pair is not registered
│       └── It should revert with OraclePairNotRegistered
└── Given caller does not have ADMIN_ROLE
    └── It should revert (AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount)

Oracle::isPairSupported(address _tokenA, address _tokenB)
├── Given pair is registered
│   └── It should return true
└── Given pair is not registered
    └── It should return false

Oracle::getSupportedPairs(address _tokenA)
├── Given token is supported
│   ├── When no pair feeds are registered
│   │   └── It should return an empty array
│   └── When pair feeds are registered
│       └── It should return the quote token addresses
└── Given token is not supported
    └── It should revert with OracleTokenNotSupported

Oracle::getPairFeedInfo(address _tokenA, address _tokenB)
├── Given pair is registered
│   ├── It should return the price feed address
│   └── It should return the staleness interval
└── Given pair is not registered
    └── It should revert with OraclePairNotRegistered

Oracle::getPairPrice(address _tokenA, address _tokenB)
├── Given pair is registered
│   ├── When the pair feed is fresh
│   │   ├── It should return the normalized pair price (18 decimals)
│   │   └── It should return updatedAt as the timestamp
│   └── When the pair feed is stale
│       └── It should revert with OracleStalePrice
└── Given pair is not registered
    └── It should revert with OraclePairNotRegistered

Oracle::getPairPriceWithStalenessCheck(address _tokenA, address _tokenB, uint256 _maxStaleness)
├── Given pair is registered
│   ├── When price is within _maxStaleness
│   │   └── It should return the normalized pair price
│   └── When price exceeds _maxStaleness
│       └── It should revert with OracleStalePrice
└── Given pair is not registered
    └── It should revert with OraclePairNotRegistered

Oracle::isTokenSupported(address _token)
├── Given token is supported
│   └── It should return true
├── Given token is not supported
│   └── It should return false
└── Given token is address(0) (native ETH) and added
    └── It should return true

Oracle::getSupportedTokens()
├── Given no tokens are supported
│   └── It should return an empty array
└── Given multiple tokens are supported
    └── It should return an array containing all supported token addresses

Oracle::getSupportedTokenCount()
├── Given no tokens are supported
│   └── It should return zero
└── Given multiple tokens are supported
    └── It should return the count of supported tokens

Oracle::getUsdFeedInfo(address _token)
├── Given token is supported
│   ├── It should return the price feed address
│   └── It should return the staleness interval
└── Given token is not supported
    └── It should revert with OracleTokenNotSupported

Oracle::Integration
└── Complete token lifecycle (test_CompleteWorkflow)
    ├── Add token with price feed
    ├── Get price (normalized to 18 decimals)
    ├── Update price feed and staleness interval
    ├── Get updated price reflecting the new feed
    ├── Verify the updated staleness interval via getUsdFeedInfo
    └── Remove token (isTokenSupported becomes false)

Oracle::Fuzz Testing
├── testFuzz_GetUsdPriceWithStalenessCheck(maxStaleness)
│   ├── When maxStaleness >= elapsed time since updatedAt
│   │   └── It should return the normalized price
│   └── When maxStaleness < elapsed time
│       └── It should revert with OracleStalePrice
├── testFuzz_AddMultipleTokens(tokenCount in 1..10)
│   ├── It should report the correct supported token count
│   └── It should return all tokens from getSupportedTokens
├── testFuzz_UpdateUsdFeedInfo_RevertInvalidFeedDecimals(decimals > 18)
│   └── It should revert with OracleInvalidFeedDecimals
├── testFuzz_PriceBoundaries(price in 1e8..1e15)
│   └── It should return a normalized price greater than zero
├── testFuzz_TimestampBoundaries(timeOffset in 0..730 days)
│   ├── When pastTimestamp == 0
│   │   └── It should revert with OracleNoRoundData
│   ├── When elapsed time exceeds the staleness interval
│   │   └── It should revert with OracleStalePrice
│   └── Otherwise
│       └── It should return a valid price
├── testFuzz_StalenessInterval(interval in 60..86400)
│   └── It should return a valid price after re-adding the token with the interval
├── testFuzz_MultiplePriceUpdates(numUpdates in 1..100)
│   └── It should return a valid price after each update
└── testFuzz_PriceFeedDecimals(decimals in 0..18)
    └── It should return a normalized price greater than zero
